cals actually bring their families"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"What’s inside"}]},{"type":"list","style":"bulleted","children":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"13 spots across breakfast, lunch, dinner, and dessert"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Practical parent intel you won’t find on any review site"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Google Maps pin list for easy navigation with a car seat in tow"}]}]}]}]}},"blocks":{}},"content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"s1"},{"type":"block","item":"s2"},{"type":"block","item":"s3"},{"type":"block","item":"s4"},{"type":"block","item":"t1"}]}},"blocks":{"s1":{"_type":"section","title":"Breakfast & Brunch","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"7a57cc8sy9"},{"type":"block","item":"qpa21pimy5"},{"type":"block","item":"ra9eehfw56"}]}},"blocks":{"7a57cc8sy9":{"_type":"venue","name":"Sandholt Bakery","address":"Laugavegur 36","description":"Kids eat free here — that alone earns it a spot. But it’s also just a lovely bakery. Sourdough, flaky pastries, and a cozy sit-in area. Grab a cinnamon roll for the toddler and a proper coffee for yourself. Mornings are calm before 9AM; after that it gets busy.","note":"Kids eat free. Highchairs available.","time":null,"is_free":1,"location":{"latitude":64.145,"longitude":-21.926},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 07:30-18:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Sandholt+Laugavegur+36+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":"Best Bakery 2025 — Reykjavík Grapevine","grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"qpa21pimy5":{"_type":"venue","name":"Laundromat Café","address":"Austurstræti 9","description":"The secret weapon: a basement play area filled with toys, books, and pillows. Drop the kids down there and enjoy your brunch in relative peace. Weekend brunch has pancakes, eggs, bacon, and fruit smoothies. Board games for the older ones.","note":"Basement play area. Weekend brunch Sat-Sun 09:00-15:00.","time":null,"is_free":1,"location":{"latitude":64.1474,"longitude":-21.9387},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 08:00-23:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Laundromat+Café+Austurstræti+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"ra9eehfw56":{"_type":"venue","name":"Brauð & Co","address":"Frakkastígur 16","description":"Opens at 6:30AM for the early risers (or the parents who had no choice). Cinnamon buns the size of your toddler’s head. Pretzel croissants that keep little hands busy. Quick in-and-out — perfect for grabbing pastries before a walk around the pond.","note":"Takeaway-friendly. No real seating for lingering with kids.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.144,"longitude":-21.9261},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Brauð+Co+Frakkastígur+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"f6ywdroy2t"}}}},"s2":{"_type":"section","title":"Lunch","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"am9kmw8v0s"},{"type":"block","item":"6dqrmfpjd5"},{"type":"block","item":"2mfpcb8wu4"},{"type":"block","item":"lapoblana"},{"type":"block","item":"plantan"}]}},"blocks":{"am9kmw8v0s":{"_type":"venue","name":"Le Kock","address":"Tryggvagata 14","description":"Sister restaurant to DEIG, and one of the most naturally family-friendly spots downtown. Legendary burgers in DEIG-made potato brioche buns. The space is relaxed, the staff are patient, and the food is genuinely good.","note":"Highchairs available. Spacious enough for prams.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1501,"longitude":-21.9434},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-22:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Le+Kock+Tryggvagata+Reykjavik","website":"lekock.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"6dqrmfpjd5":{"_type":"venue","name":"Kaffi Lækur","address":"Laugarnesvegur 75","description":"A neighbourhood gem popular with new parents. Dedicated kids’ corner with toys and books. Sourdough flatbakes are hearty and delicious. Slightly off the tourist path.","note":"Kids’ corner with toys and books.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1422,"longitude":-21.9058},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Kaffi+L%C3%A6kur+Laugarnesvegur+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"2mfpcb8wu4":{"_type":"venue","name":"Chickpea","address":"Hallveigarstígur 1","description":"Family-run vegetarian spot with the best falafel in town. Generous portions, freshly made, warm and unhurried vibe. Great for kids who like wraps and hummus.","note":"Vegetarian/vegan. Casual and quick.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1457,"longitude":-21.9341},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 10:00-20:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Chickpea+Reykjavik","website":"chickpea.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"e59v159sv3"},"lapoblana":{"_type":"venue","name":"La Poblana","address":"Laugavegur 12, 2nd floor","description":"Authentic Mexican tacos on the second floor of Laugavegur 12. Family-run, using recipes from Puebla. Tacos are perfect kid food — small, handheld, customisable. Vegetarian and gluten-free options if your little one has restrictions. Warm, unhurried vibe.","note":"Family-run. Vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free options.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1468,"longitude":-21.9308},"opening_hours":"Su-Th 12:00-21:00; Fr-Sa 12:00-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/La+Poblana+Laugavegur+Reykjavik","website":"lapoblana.is","phone":"760 7221","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"plantan":{"_type":"venue","name":"Plantan Bistro (Norræna húsið)","address":"Sturlugata 5","description":"Plant-based bistro inside the Nordic House — an Alvar Aalto-designed cultural gem. Come for lunch, stay for the library. The kids’ section has children’s literature in Nordic languages, a play area, and storytelling hours in winter. Free library card. Perfect rainy-day combo: eat, read, explore.","note":"Nordic House library with dedicated kids’ section, play area, and storytelling hours. Open Tue–Sun.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.142,"longitude":-21.9508},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:00-17:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Plantan+Bistro+Norraena+husid+Reykjavik","website":"plantankaffihus.is","phone":"551 7030","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"s3":{"_type":"section","title":"Dinner","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"4bpssf44nj"},{"type":"block","item":"r091s3bmwq"},{"type":"block","item":"twoguys"},{"type":"block","item":"justwinginit"}]}},"blocks":{"4bpssf44nj":{"_type":"venue","name":"Búllan","address":"Höfði (Bolholt 6)","description":"The Höfði location is the one you want with kids. Walls covered in drawings done by children during meals — your kids can add to the collection. No-frills burgers, zero pretension.","note":"Höfði location best for families. Kids’ drawings on walls.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1355,"longitude":-21.9029},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/B%C3%BAllan+H%C3%B6f%C3%B0i+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"r091s3bmwq":{"_type":"venue","name":"Jómfrúin","address":"Lækjargata 4","description":"Classic Danish smørrebrød — open-faced sandwiches perfect for kids who like to pick and choose toppings. Best service in town means they’ll be patient with your order taking twice as long.","note":"Best service in town. Patient with families.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1468,"longitude":-21.9374},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-22:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/J%C3%B3mfr%C3%BAin+L%C3%A6kjargata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":"551 0100","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"qzs1eqbdl3"},"twoguys":{"_type":"venue","name":"Two Guys","address":"Laugavegur 105 (Hlemmur)","description":"Award-winning burgers at Hlemmur — voted Best Burger in Reykjavík four years running. They have a proper kids’ menu: Klemma burger, fries and juice for 1,500 ISK. The vibe is relaxed enough that nobody bats an eye at a messy eater. Great veggie options too.","note":"Kids’ menu available (1,500 ISK). Best Burger 2023–2026.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1428,"longitude":-21.9148},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/2guys+Laugavegur+105+Reykjavik","website":"2guys.is","phone":"790 2323","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"justwinginit":{"_type":"venue","name":"Just Wing’in It","address":"Snorrabraut 56","description":"Over 30 wing flavours plus chicken tenders for the less adventurous. The real draw for kids: corn hole tossing and shuffleboard to keep them busy while you eat. Casual, loud, zero judgement — basically designed for families even if they didn’t mean to be.","note":"Games for kids (corn hole, shuffleboard). Takeaway available.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.143,"longitude":-21.915},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Just+Wingin+It+Snorrabraut+Reykjavik","website":"justwinginit.is","phone":"661 2878","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"s4":{"_type":"section","title":"Sweet Treats & Ice Cream","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"3gt0bkcr5j"}]}},"blocks":{"3gt0bkcr5j":{"_type":"venue","name":"DEIG Workshop","address":"Tryggvagata 14","description":"Doughnuts and bagels made fresh daily. The doughnuts are the obvious kid-magnet, but don’t sleep on the bagels. Perfect post-playground bribe.","note":"Right next to Le Kock — easy to combine visits.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1501,"longitude":-21.9434},"opening_hours":"Mo-Fr 07:00-17:00; Sa-Su 08:00-16:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/DEIG+Workshop+Tryggvagata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"t1":{"_type":"text_block","heading":"Tips for Eating Out with Kids in Reykjavík","is_free":1,"content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Icelanders eat late.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Dinner service starts at 17:00–18:00. If you go right when doors open, you’ll often have the place to yourself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Most places have highchairs.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" But they’re often the basic IKEA kind. If your child needs a specific setup, bring your own clip-on seat."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Changing tables are rare.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Outside of the bigger restaurants and shopping centres, you’ll mostly be improvising."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Don’t stress about the kids.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Reykjavík is extremely child-friendly as a culture. Nobody’s going to glare at you if your toddler is being a toddler."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Book ahead for dinner.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" The best places are small. Mentioning you’re bringing kids when you book helps them seat you somewhere with more space."}]}]}},"blocks":{}}}}}}','2026-03-23T22:17:28.442Z','publish','editor','Sunna','etid_67388504-dc4b-4b53-aa82-48f6b1964253');
