 2015, having worked alongside his father since 2003. The handover was seamless — the same recipes, the same standards, the same unhurried pace. Walking into Jómfrúin today feels, as the Grapevine once put it, like being \"transported to 1985 Reykjavík.\" The wood-panelled interior hasn''t changed much. Neither has the quality."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"In a city where restaurants open and close with the seasons, Jómfrúin has been a constant for nearly thirty years. It''s the kind of place where the staff know the regulars, where the portions haven''t shrunk, and where nobody''s trying to reinvent anything. The smørrebrød is the same as it was when Jakob Sr. first laid rye bread on a board here — and that''s exactly the point."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"The details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Jómfrúin is open daily for lunch and dinner. Reservations aren''t strictly necessary for weekday lunch, but weekend afternoons — especially during jazz season — fill up fast. The restaurant is at "},{"type":"span","value":"Lækjargata 4","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":", close to the City Hall, Alþingi, and the bottom of Laugavegur."}]}]}}}','2026-03-24T16:49:42.060Z','restore','editor','Sunna','etid_e8b998aa-9d36-4617-a2dc-13f1d4280c67');
INSERT INTO "record_versions" ("id","model_api_key","record_id","version_number","snapshot","created_at","action","actor_type","actor_label","actor_token_id") VALUES('6jaels0rpp','editorial','fyuw66y28x',6,'{"title":"Jómfrúin: The Maiden of Lækjargata","slug":"jomfruin","excerpt":"How an Icelandic man trained under Copenhagen''s smørrebrød royalty and brought the craft to Reykjavík — where it''s been a Saturday afternoon institution for nearly thirty years.","date":"2026-03-23","image":"1zb4ixb1xa","content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Every Saturday afternoon from June through August, a back garden on Lækjargata fills with the sound of live jazz. People sit in the sun with plates of open-faced sandwiches and cold Icelandic beer. This is Jómfrúin — and it''s been doing this since 1996."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"From Copenhagen to Lækjargata"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"The story starts in 1888, at Oscar Davidsen''s legendary smørrebrød restaurant in Copenhagen — a place so famous its menu was once listed in the Guinness Book of Records as the longest in the world. Generations later, Ida Davidsen inherited the restaurant and continued the tradition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"In the early 1990s, an Icelandic restaurateur named Jakob Jakobsson trained under Ida Davidsen — becoming the first man in the world to graduate as a "},{"type":"span","value":"smørrebrødsjomfru","marks":["emphasis"]},{"type":"span","value":", the traditional title for a master of open-faced sandwich preparation. The word translates roughly to \"smørrebrød maiden,\" and it had always been held by women. Jakob broke the mould."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"He brought the craft back to Reykjavík and opened Jómfrúin — \"The Maiden\" — on Lækjargata in 1996. The restaurant sits right in the heart of downtown, a few steps from the parliament building and Tjörnin pond."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"What you''re eating"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Smørrebrød is deceptively simple: a single slice of dark rye bread, buttered, and then piled with toppings arranged with care. At Jómfrúin the classics are all here — pickled herring with onion, smoked salmon with capers, roast beef with remoulade and crispy onions, and the famous "},{"type":"span","value":"rækjupíramídi","marks":["emphasis"]},{"type":"span","value":" (shrimp pyramid!): a towering pyramid of shrimp on a sliver of bread that has become one of the most photographed dishes in Reykjavík."}]},{"type":"block","item":"img_frikadeller"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"The sandwiches are priced whole or half — and that''s the key to eating here well. You don''t commit to one enormous sandwich. You pick two halves, mix and match, and build your own lunch. The menu of the day always has pairing suggestions if you''re short on ideas, but here are ours: HC Andersen, Danish Adventure, Roast Beef Modern, Smoked Salmon, and Shrimp & Egg. Two halves, one plate, no regrets."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Beyond the sandwiches, the warm dishes hold their own. "},{"type":"span","value":"Biksemad","marks":["emphasis"]},{"type":"span","value":" — a hash of diced meat and potatoes topped with a fried egg and pickled beets — is comfort food of the highest order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"The Reykjavík Grapevine''s 2015 Best of Reykjavík panel described the "},{"type":"span","value":"rækjupíramídi","marks":["emphasis"]},{"type":"span","value":" as an \"honest-to-god pyramid of shrimp,\" and called out the \"Hangover\" — roast beef on rye with tomatoes, horseradish, and a fried egg — as a must-order."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"Ákavíti if you''re feeling cheeky"}]},{"type":"block","item":"img_akaviti"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"The fridge behind the bar is stocked with schnapps — ákavíti in Icelandic — and if you''re having the herring or the shrimp, a small cold glass alongside pairs nicely. It''s a tradition borrowed directly from Denmark, and Jómfrúin takes it seriously."}]},{"type":"block","item":"img_drinks"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"The Saturday jazz"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Since its opening year, Jómfrúin has hosted live jazz every Saturday afternoon in summer. Sigurður Flosason, one of Iceland''s most respected jazz musicians, curates the programme. The concerts run from 3 PM to 5 PM, admission is free, and they take place on Jómfrúartorg — the small square behind the restaurant. Check "},{"type":"link","url":"https://jomfruin.is/summar-jazz/","children":[{"type":"span","value":"jomfruin.is/summar-jazz"}]},{"type":"span","value":" for the schedule."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"What started as a casual summer tradition has become one of Reykjavík''s most beloved cultural rituals. The series has grown so popular it won the Icelandic Music Awards for Best Event. Arrive early if you want a seat — by 3 PM on a sunny Saturday, the garden is packed."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"Christmas at Jómfrúin"}]},{"type":"block","item":"img_christmas"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Christmas is when Jómfrúin transforms. Families — sometimes groups of twenty or more — book the long tables months in advance. The platters come out piled high: mixed smørrebrød, warm dishes, beer, and schnapps. It has become a Reykjavík tradition for many families to gather here in December, and the restaurant books up fast. If you''re planning a Christmas lunch, call early."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"Still a family affair"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Jakob''s son, Jakob Jr., took over as manager in 2015, having worked alongside his father since 2003. The handover was seamless — the same recipes, the same standards, the same unhurried pace. Walking into Jómfrúin today feels, as the Grapevine once put it, like being \"transported to 1985 Reykjavík.\" The wood-panelled interior hasn''t changed much. Neither has the quality."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"In a city where restaurants open and close with the seasons, Jómfrúin has been a constant for nearly thirty years. It''s the kind of place where the staff know the regulars, where the portions haven''t shrunk, and where nobody''s trying to reinvent anything. The smørrebrød is the same as it was when Jakob Sr. first laid rye bread on a board here — and that''s exactly the point."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"The details"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Jómfrúin is open daily for lunch and dinner. Reservations aren''t strictly necessary for weekday lunch, but weekend afternoons — especially during jazz season — fill up fast. The restaurant is at "},{"type":"span","value":"Lækjargata 4","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":", close to the City Hall, Alþingi, and the bottom of Laugavegur."}]}]}},"blocks":{"img_frikadeller":{"_type":"image_block","image":"aizi9qhzmy","caption":"Smoked salmon with scrambled eggs, and roast beef smørrebrød."},"img_akaviti":{"_type":"image_block","image":"xd8fcqtfm3","caption":"The ákavíti fridge. They take their schnapps seriously."},"img_drinks":{"_type":"image_block","image":"e81xdey4dz","caption":"Tuborg Classic and schnapps glasses. The proper way to wash down smørrebrød."},"img_christmas":{"_type":"image_block","image":"5uqq7vitni","caption":"The full Christmas spread — mixed smørrebrød platter, beer, and schnapps. This is what December looks like at Jómfrúin."}}}}','2026-03-24T16:57:47.800Z','publish','editor','Sunna','etid_e8b998aa-9d36-4617-a2dc-13f1d4280c67');
INSERT INTO "record_versions" ("id","model_api_key","record_id","version_number","snapshot","created_at","action","actor_type","actor_label","actor_token_id") VALUES('mtrrpjgcx1','guide','7guc0nxad6',6,'{"title":"Reykjavík with Kids","slug":"reykjavik-with-kids","subtitle":"Where to eat when you''ve got little ones in tow","description":"A local parent''s guide to eating out with kids in Reykjavík. Play areas, high chairs, patient staff, and food that makes everyone happy — including you. Updated for 2026.","price":10,"gumroad_product_id":"reykjavik-with-kids","gumroad_url":"https://rvkfoodie.gumroad.com/l/reykjavik-with-kids","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/placelists/list/reykjavik-kids-food","intro":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Reykjavík is surprisingly great for eating out with kids — if you know where to go. This guide is for parents who want to eat well without sacrificing their sanity or settling for chicken nuggets.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"Why this guide"}]},{"type":"list","style":"bulleted","children":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Written by a local parent who eats out constantly — every place here has been tested with actual children"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Honest notes on high chairs, pram space, play areas, and changing facilities"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"What to order for picky eaters AND what the parents should get"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Timing tips — when to go to avoid the chaos"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"No tourist traps, no chain restaurants — just places locals actually bring their families"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"What’s inside"}]},{"type":"list","style":"bulleted","children":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"15 spots across breakfast, lunch, dinner, and dessert"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Practical parent intel you won’t find on any review site"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Google Maps pin list for easy navigation with a car seat in tow"}]}]}]}]}},"blocks":{}},"content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"s1"},{"type":"block","item":"s2"},{"type":"block","item":"s3"},{"type":"block","item":"s4"},{"type":"block","item":"t1"}]}},"blocks":{"s1":{"_type":"section","title":"Breakfast & Brunch","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"7a57cc8sy9"},{"type":"block","item":"qpa21pimy5"},{"type":"block","item":"ra9eehfw56"}]}},"blocks":{"7a57cc8sy9":{"_type":"venue","name":"Sandholt Bakery","address":"Laugavegur 36","description":"Kids eat free here — that alone earns it a spot. But it’s also just a lovely bakery. Sourdough, flaky pastries, and a cozy sit-in area. Grab a cinnamon roll for the toddler and a proper coffee for yourself. Mornings are calm before 9AM; after that it gets busy.","note":"Kids eat free. Highchairs available.","time":null,"is_free":1,"location":{"latitude":64.145,"longitude":-21.926},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 07:30-18:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Sandholt+Laugavegur+36+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":"Best Bakery 2025 — Reykjavík Grapevine","grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"qpa21pimy5":{"_type":"venue","name":"Laundromat Café","address":"Austurstræti 9","description":"The secret weapon: a basement play area filled with toys, books, and pillows. Drop the kids down there and enjoy your brunch in relative peace. Weekend brunch has pancakes, eggs, bacon, and fruit smoothies. Board games for the older ones.","note":"Basement play area. Weekend brunch Sat-Sun 09:00-15:00.","time":null,"is_free":1,"location":{"latitude":64.1474,"longitude":-21.9387},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 08:00-23:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Laundromat+Café+Austurstræti+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"ra9eehfw56":{"_type":"venue","name":"Brauð & Co","address":"Frakkastígur 16","description":"Opens at 6:30AM for the early risers (or the parents who had no choice). Cinnamon buns the size of your toddler’s head. Pretzel croissants that keep little hands busy. Quick in-and-out — perfect for grabbing pastries before a walk around the pond.","note":"Takeaway-friendly. No real seating for lingering with kids.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.144,"longitude":-21.9261},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Brauð+Co+Frakkastígur+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"f6ywdroy2t"}}}},"s2":{"_type":"section","title":"Lunch","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"am9kmw8v0s"},{"type":"block","item":"6dqrmfpjd5"},{"type":"block","item":"2mfpcb8wu4"},{"type":"block","item":"lapoblana"},{"type":"block","item":"plantan"}]}},"blocks":{"am9kmw8v0s":{"_type":"venue","name":"Le Kock","address":"Tryggvagata 14","description":"Sister restaurant to DEIG, and one of the most naturally family-friendly spots downtown. Legendary burgers in DEIG-made potato brioche buns. The space is relaxed, the staff are patient, and the food is genuinely good.","note":"Highchairs available. Spacious enough for prams.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1501,"longitude":-21.9434},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-22:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Le+Kock+Tryggvagata+Reykjavik","website":"lekock.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"6dqrmfpjd5":{"_type":"venue","name":"Kaffi Lækur","address":"Laugarnesvegur 75","description":"A neighbourhood gem popular with new parents. Dedicated kids’ corner with toys and books. Sourdough flatbakes are hearty and delicious. Slightly off the tourist path.","note":"Kids’ corner with toys and books.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1422,"longitude":-21.9058},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Kaffi+L%C3%A6kur+Laugarnesvegur+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"2mfpcb8wu4":{"_type":"venue","name":"Chickpea","address":"Hallveigarstígur 1","description":"Family-run vegetarian spot with the best falafel in town. Generous portions, freshly made, warm and unhurried vibe. Great for kids who like wraps and hummus.","note":"Vegetarian/vegan. Casual and quick.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1457,"longitude":-21.9341},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 10:00-20:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Chickpea+Reykjavik","website":"chickpea.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"e59v159sv3"},"lapoblana":{"_type":"venue","name":"La Poblana","address":"Laugavegur 12, 2nd floor","description":"Authentic Mexican tacos on the second floor of Laugavegur 12. Family-run, using recipes from Puebla. Tacos are perfect kid food — small, handheld, customisable. Vegetarian and gluten-free options if your little one has restrictions. Warm, unhurried vibe.","note":"Family-run. Vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free options.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1468,"longitude":-21.9308},"opening_hours":"Su-Th 12:00-21:00; Fr-Sa 12:00-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/La+Poblana+Laugavegur+Reykjavik","website":"lapoblana.is","phone":"760 7221","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"plantan":{"_type":"venue","name":"Plantan Bistro (Norræna húsið)","address":"Sturlugata 5","description":"Plant-based bistro inside the Nordic House — an Alvar Aalto-designed cultural gem. Come for lunch, stay for the library. The kids’ section has children’s literature in Nordic languages, a play area, and storytelling hours in winter. Free library card. Perfect rainy-day combo: eat, read, explore.","note":"Nordic House library with dedicated kids’ section, play area, and storytelling hours. Open Tue–Sun.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.142,"longitude":-21.9508},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:00-17:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Plantan+Bistro+Norraena+husid+Reykjavik","website":"plantankaffihus.is","phone":"551 7030","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"s3":{"_type":"section","title":"Dinner","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"bullan"},{"type":"block","item":"r091s3bmwq"},{"type":"block","item":"twoguys"},{"type":"block","item":"justwinginit"}]}},"blocks":{"bullan":{"_type":"venue","name":"Búllan","address":"Geirsgata 1","description":"Multiple locations around town, but the Geirsgata spot by the old harbour is the one most visitors will hit first. No-frills burgers, zero pretension, walls covered in kids’ drawings — your kids can add to the collection. The Höfði branch (Bolholt 6) is perfect if you’re on your way out of town.","note":"Multiple locations. Geirsgata for downtown, Höfði (Bolholt 6) on the way out of town.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1512,"longitude":-21.9443},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/B%C3%BAllan+Geirsgata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"r091s3bmwq":{"_type":"venue","name":"Jómfrúin","address":"Lækjargata 4","description":"Classic Danish smørrebrød — open-faced sandwiches perfect for kids who like to pick and choose toppings. Best service in town means they’ll be patient with your order taking twice as long.","note":"Best service in town. Patient with families.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1468,"longitude":-21.9374},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-22:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/J%C3%B3mfr%C3%BAin+L%C3%A6kjargata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":"551 0100","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"qzs1eqbdl3"},"twoguys":{"_type":"venue","name":"2guys","address":"Laugavegur 105 (Hlemmur)","description":"Award-winning burgers at Hlemmur — voted Best Burger in Reykjavík four years running. They have a proper kids’ menu: Klemma burger, fries and juice for 1,500 ISK. The vibe is relaxed enough that nobody bats an eye at a messy eater. Great veggie options too.","note":"Kids’ menu available (1,500 ISK). Best Burger 2023–2026.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1428,"longitude":-21.9148},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/2guys+Laugavegur+105+Reykjavik","website":"2guys.is","phone":"790 2323","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"justwinginit":{"_type":"venue","name":"Just Wing’in It","address":"Snorrabraut 56","description":"Over 30 wing flavours plus chicken tenders for the less adventurous. The real draw for kids: corn hole tossing and shuffleboard to keep them busy while you eat. Casual, loud, zero judgement — basically designed for families even if they didn’t mean to be.","note":"Games for kids (corn hole, shuffleboard). Takeaway available.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.143,"longitude":-21.915},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Just+Wingin+It+Snorrabraut+Reykjavik","website":"justwinginit.is","phone":"661 2878","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"s4":{"_type":"section","title":"Sweet Treats & Ice Cream","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"3gt0bkcr5j"},{"type":"block","item":"mokka"},{"type":"block","item":"gaeta"}]}},"blocks":{"3gt0bkcr5j":{"_type":"venue","name":"DEIG Workshop","address":"Tryggvagata 14","description":"Doughnuts and bagels made fresh daily. The doughnuts are the obvious kid-magnet, but don’t sleep on the bagels. Perfect post-playground bribe.","note":"Right next to Le Kock — easy to combine visits.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1501,"longitude":-21.9434},"opening_hours":"Mo-Fr 07:00-17:00; Sa-Su 08:00-16:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/DEIG+Workshop+Tryggvagata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"mokka":{"_type":"venue","name":"Mokka Kaffi","address":"Skólavörðustígur 3a","description":"Open since 1958 and barely changed since — red carpet, leatherette booths, rotating art on the walls. The waffles with cream and jam are the reason you’re here. Kids love them, you’ll love the espresso (Mokka was the first café in Iceland to serve it). A Reykjavík institution.","note":"Open since 1958. Famous waffles with cream and jam.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1441,"longitude":-21.9278},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 09:00-18:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Mokka+Kaffi+Sk%C3%B3lav%C3%B6r%C3%B0ust%C3%ADgur+Reykjavik","website":"mokka.is","phone":"552 1174","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"gaeta":{"_type":"venue","name":"Gaeta Gelato","address":"Aðalstræti 6 (Ingólfstorg)","description":"Proper Italian gelato made fresh daily on Ingólfstorg. Pistachio, salted caramel, and seasonal flavours — plus cannoli and tiramisu if the kids want to branch out. The owners have nearly 25 years of experience as gelato makers. Open late, perfect for a post-dinner stroll.","note":"Fresh gelato daily. Open until 23:00.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1477,"longitude":-21.9399},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 12:30-23:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Gaeta+Gelato+Ingolfstorg+Reykjavik","website":"gelato.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"t1":{"_type":"text_block","heading":"Tips for Eating Out with Kids in Reykjavík","is_free":1,"content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Icelanders eat late.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Dinner service starts at 17:00–18:00. If you go right when doors open, you’ll often have the place to yourself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Most places have highchairs.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" But they’re often the basic IKEA kind. If your child needs a specific setup, bring your own clip-on seat."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Changing tables are rare.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Outside of the bigger restaurants and shopping centres, you’ll mostly be improvising."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Don’t stress about the kids.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Reykjavík is extremely child-friendly as a culture. Nobody’s going to glare at you if your toddler is being a toddler."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Book ahead for dinner.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" The best places are small. Mentioning you’re bringing kids when you book helps them seat you somewhere with more space."}]}]}},"blocks":{}}}}}}','2026-03-24T17:10:27.722Z','publish','editor','Sunna','etid_67388504-dc4b-4b53-aa82-48f6b1964253');
INSERT INTO "record_versions" ("id","model_api_key","record_id","version_number","snapshot","created_at","action","actor_type","actor_label","actor_token_id") VALUES('owlhsfrc0x','guide','7guc0nxad6',7,'{"title":"Reykjavík with Kids","slug":"reykjavik-with-kids","subtitle":"Where to eat when you''ve got little ones in tow","description":"A local parent''s guide to eating out with kids in Reykjavík. Play areas, high chairs, patient staff, and food that makes everyone happy — including you. Updated for 2026.","price":10,"gumroad_product_id":"reykjavik-with-kids","gumroad_url":"https://rvkfoodie.gumroad.com/l/reykjavik-with-kids","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/placelists/list/reykjavik-kids-food","intro":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Reykjavík is surprisingly great for eating out with kids — if you know where to go. This guide is for parents who want to eat well without sacrificing their sanity or settling for chicken nuggets.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"Why this guide"}]},{"type":"list","style":"bulleted","children":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Written by a local parent who eats out constantly — every place here has been tested with actual children"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Honest notes on high chairs, pram space, play areas, and changing facilities"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"What to order for picky eaters AND what the parents should get"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Timing tips — when to go to avoid the chaos"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"No tourist traps, no chain restaurants — just places locals actually bring their families"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"children":[{"type":"span","value":"What’s inside"}]},{"type":"list","style":"bulleted","children":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"15 spots across breakfast, lunch, dinner, and dessert"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Practical parent intel you won’t find on any review site"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Google Maps pin list for easy navigation with a car seat in tow"}]}]}]}]}},"blocks":{}},"content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"sec1"},{"type":"block","item":"sec2"},{"type":"block","item":"sec3"},{"type":"block","item":"sec4"},{"type":"block","item":"tip1"}]}},"blocks":{"sec1":{"_type":"section","title":"Breakfast & Brunch","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"v_sandholt"},{"type":"block","item":"v_laundromat"},{"type":"block","item":"v_braud"}]}},"blocks":{"v_sandholt":{"_type":"venue","name":"Sandholt Bakery","address":"Laugavegur 36","description":"Kids eat free here — that alone earns it a spot. But it’s also just a lovely bakery. Sourdough, flaky pastries, and a cozy sit-in area. Grab a cinnamon roll for the toddler and a proper coffee for yourself. Mornings are calm before 9AM; after that it gets busy.","note":"Kids eat free. Highchairs available.","time":null,"is_free":1,"location":{"latitude":64.145,"longitude":-21.926},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 07:30-18:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Sandholt+Laugavegur+36+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":"Best Bakery 2025 — Reykjavík Grapevine","grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"v_laundromat":{"_type":"venue","name":"Laundromat Café","address":"Austurstræti 9","description":"The secret weapon: a basement play area filled with toys, books, and pillows. Drop the kids down there and enjoy your brunch in relative peace. Weekend brunch has pancakes, eggs, bacon, and fruit smoothies. Board games for the older ones.","note":"Basement play area. Weekend brunch Sat-Sun 09:00-15:00.","time":null,"is_free":1,"location":{"latitude":64.1474,"longitude":-21.9387},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 08:00-23:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Laundromat+Café+Austurstræti+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"v_braud":{"_type":"venue","name":"Brauð & Co","address":"Frakkastígur 16","description":"Opens at 6:30AM for the early risers (or the parents who had no choice). Cinnamon buns the size of your toddler’s head. Pretzel croissants that keep little hands busy. Quick in-and-out — perfect for grabbing pastries before a walk around the pond.","note":"Takeaway-friendly. No real seating for lingering with kids.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.144,"longitude":-21.9261},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Brau%C3%B0+Co+Frakkast%C3%ADgur+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"f6ywdroy2t"}}}},"sec2":{"_type":"section","title":"Lunch","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"v_lekock"},{"type":"block","item":"v_kaffilaekur"},{"type":"block","item":"v_chickpea"},{"type":"block","item":"v_lapoblana"},{"type":"block","item":"v_plantan"}]}},"blocks":{"v_lekock":{"_type":"venue","name":"Le Kock","address":"Tryggvagata 14","description":"Sister restaurant to DEIG, and one of the most naturally family-friendly spots downtown. Legendary burgers in DEIG-made potato brioche buns. The space is relaxed, the staff are patient, and the food is genuinely good.","note":"Highchairs available. Spacious enough for prams.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1501,"longitude":-21.9434},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-22:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Le+Kock+Tryggvagata+Reykjavik","website":"lekock.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"u0vmbb8plv"},"v_kaffilaekur":{"_type":"venue","name":"Kaffi Lækur","address":"Laugarnesvegur 75","description":"A neighbourhood gem popular with new parents. Dedicated kids’ corner with toys and books. Sourdough flatbakes are hearty and delicious. Slightly off the tourist path.","note":"Kids’ corner with toys and books.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1422,"longitude":-21.9058},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Kaffi+L%C3%A6kur+Laugarnesvegur+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"v_chickpea":{"_type":"venue","name":"Chickpea","address":"Hallveigastígur 1","description":"Family-run vegetarian spot with the best falafel in town. Generous portions, freshly made, warm and unhurried vibe. Great for kids who like wraps and hummus.","note":"Vegetarian/vegan. Casual and quick.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1457,"longitude":-21.9341},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 10:00-20:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Chickpea+Reykjavik","website":"chickpea.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"e59v159sv3"},"v_lapoblana":{"_type":"venue","name":"La Poblana","address":"Laugavegur 12, 2nd floor","description":"Authentic Mexican food on the second floor of Laugavegur 12. Family-run, using recipes from Puebla. Way more than just tacos — enchiladas in salsa verde, quesadillas, burritos, and plenty of other dishes. Everything is customisable and most items work great as kid food: small portions, handheld, easy to share. Vegetarian and gluten-free options if your little one has restrictions. Warm, unhurried vibe.","note":"Family-run. Full Mexican menu beyond tacos. Vegetarian, vegan and gluten-free options.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1468,"longitude":-21.9308},"opening_hours":"Su-Th 12:00-21:00; Fr-Sa 12:00-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/La+Poblana+Laugavegur+Reykjavik","website":"lapoblana.is","phone":"760 7221","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"vcoeds1fhd"},"v_plantan":{"_type":"venue","name":"Plantan Bistro (Norræna húsið)","address":"Sturlugata 5","description":"Plant-based bistro inside the Nordic House — an Alvar Aalto-designed cultural gem. Come for lunch, stay for the library. The kids’ section has children’s literature in Nordic languages, a play area, and storytelling hours in winter. Free library card. Perfect rainy-day combo: eat, read, explore.","note":"Nordic House library with dedicated kids’ section, play area, and storytelling hours. Open Tue–Sun.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.142,"longitude":-21.9508},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:00-17:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Plantan+Bistro+Norraena+husid+Reykjavik","website":"plantankaffihus.is","phone":"551 7030","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"sec3":{"_type":"section","title":"Dinner","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"v_bullan"},{"type":"block","item":"v_jomfruin"},{"type":"block","item":"v_twoguys"},{"type":"block","item":"v_justwinginit"}]}},"blocks":{"v_bullan":{"_type":"venue","name":"Búllan","address":"Geirsgata 1","description":"Multiple locations around town, but the Geirsgata spot by the old harbour is the one most visitors will hit first. No-frills burgers, zero pretension, walls covered in kids’ drawings — your kids can add to the collection. The Höfði branch (Bolholt 6) is perfect if you’re on your way out of town.","note":"Multiple locations. Geirsgata for downtown, Höfði (Bolholt 6) on the way out of town.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1512,"longitude":-21.9443},"opening_hours":null,"google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/B%C3%BAllan+Geirsgata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"824a2ky58f"},"v_jomfruin":{"_type":"venue","name":"Jómfrúin","address":"Lækjargata 4","description":"Classic Danish smørrebrød — open-faced sandwiches perfect for kids who like to pick and choose toppings. Best service in town means they’ll be patient with your order taking twice as long.","note":"Best service in town. Patient with families.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1468,"longitude":-21.9374},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-22:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/J%C3%B3mfr%C3%BAin+L%C3%A6kjargata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":"551 0100","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":"qzs1eqbdl3"},"v_twoguys":{"_type":"venue","name":"2guys","address":"Laugavegur 105 (Hlemmur)","description":"Award-winning burgers at Hlemmur — voted Best Burger in Reykjavík four years running. They have a proper kids’ menu: Klemma burger, fries and juice for 1,500 ISK. The vibe is relaxed enough that nobody bats an eye at a messy eater. Great veggie options too.","note":"Kids’ menu available (1,500 ISK). Best Burger 2023–2026.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1428,"longitude":-21.9148},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/2guys+Laugavegur+105+Reykjavik","website":"2guys.is","phone":"790 2323","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"v_justwinginit":{"_type":"venue","name":"Just Wing’in It","address":"Snorrabraut 56","description":"Over 30 wing flavours plus chicken tenders for the less adventurous. The real draw for kids: corn hole tossing and shuffleboard to keep them busy while you eat. Casual, loud, zero judgement — basically designed for families even if they didn’t mean to be.","note":"Games for kids (corn hole, shuffleboard). Takeaway available.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.143,"longitude":-21.915},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 11:30-21:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Just+Wingin+It+Snorrabraut+Reykjavik","website":"justwinginit.is","phone":"661 2878","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"sec4":{"_type":"section","title":"Sweet Treats & Ice Cream","venues":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","item":"v_deig"},{"type":"block","item":"v_mokka"},{"type":"block","item":"v_gaeta"}]}},"blocks":{"v_deig":{"_type":"venue","name":"DEIG Workshop","address":"Tryggvagata 14","description":"Doughnuts and bagels made fresh daily. The doughnuts are the obvious kid-magnet, but don’t sleep on the bagels. Perfect post-playground bribe.","note":"Right next to Le Kock — easy to combine visits.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1501,"longitude":-21.9434},"opening_hours":"Mo-Fr 07:00-17:00; Sa-Su 08:00-16:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/DEIG+Workshop+Tryggvagata+Reykjavik","website":null,"phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"v_mokka":{"_type":"venue","name":"Mokka Kaffi","address":"Skólavörðustígur 3a","description":"Open since 1958 and barely changed since — red carpet, leatherette booths, rotating art on the walls. The waffles with cream and jam are the reason you’re here. Kids love them, you’ll love the espresso (Mokka was the first café in Iceland to serve it). A Reykjavík institution.","note":"Open since 1958. Famous waffles with cream and jam.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1441,"longitude":-21.9278},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 09:00-18:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Mokka+Kaffi+Sk%C3%B3lav%C3%B6r%C3%B0ust%C3%ADgur+Reykjavik","website":"mokka.is","phone":"552 1174","best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null},"v_gaeta":{"_type":"venue","name":"Gaeta Gelato","address":"Aðalstræti 6 (Ingólfstorg)","description":"Proper Italian gelato made fresh daily on Ingólfstorg. Pistachio, salted caramel, and seasonal flavours — plus cannoli and tiramisu if the kids want to branch out. The owners have nearly 25 years of experience as gelato makers. Open late, perfect for a post-dinner stroll.","note":"Fresh gelato daily. Open until 23:00.","time":null,"is_free":0,"location":{"latitude":64.1477,"longitude":-21.9399},"opening_hours":"Mo-Su 12:30-23:00","google_maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/Gaeta+Gelato+Ingolfstorg+Reykjavik","website":"gelato.is","phone":null,"best_of_award":null,"grapevine_url":null,"image":null}}}},"tip1":{"_type":"text_block","heading":"Tips for Eating Out with Kids in Reykjavík","is_free":1,"content":{"value":{"schema":"dast","document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Icelanders eat late.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Dinner service starts at 17:00–18:00. If you go right when doors open, you’ll often have the place to yourself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Most places have highchairs.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" But they’re often the basic IKEA kind. If your child needs a specific setup, bring your own clip-on seat."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Changing tables are rare.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Outside of the bigger restaurants and shopping centres, you’ll mostly be improvising."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Don’t stress about the kids.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" Reykjavík is extremely child-friendly as a culture. Nobody’s going to glare at you if your toddler is being a toddler."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"span","value":"Book ahead for dinner.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"span","value":" The best places are small. Mentioning you’re bringing kids when you book helps them seat you somewhere with more space."}]}]}},"blocks":{}}}}}}','2026-03-24T17:15:47.851Z','publish','editor','Sunna','etid_67388504-dc4b-4b53-aa82-48f6b1964253');
